The correct fix would be: on a failed attempt, allow the client to retry with a NEW idempotency key but the server should allow more than 2 total attempts, OR the server should permit re-reserving a failed attempt (delete it and allow a new one). Currently, the state service does neither. So any failed attempt permanently consumes one of the two slots. CRITICAL.

